  "example_explanation": "This example demonstrates symbol resolution and relocation implicitly.  When compiled, `function_a` and `function_b` are compiled into separate object files.  `function_b` calls `function_a` \u2013 an external reference. The linker resolves this external symbol `function_a`, linking it to the appropriate address in the compiled object file.  Relocation occurs because the linker must adjust the address of `global_var` within `function_a` and the call to `function_a` within `function_b` to reflect their final addresses in the combined executable's memory space. Without successful resolution and relocation, the program would fail to link or produce incorrect results at runtime.",
